  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda Integrated Health Systems Activity (RIHSA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Rwanda):  .The Rwanda Integrated Health Systems Activity (RIHSA) directly contributes to the Mission&apos;s Development Objective of  of improved health outcomes and its associated Intermediate Result,  &quot;Health Systems Strengthened for Increased Sustainability,&quot; as described in USAID&apos;s Country Development Cooperation Strategy, 2020-2025..RIHSA aims to improve the governance of the health system, reduce financial risk, and tailor information systems to provide information for Rwanda&apos;s health system decision-makers. RIHSA will improve management and accountability at the Ministry of Health at the central and subnational levels, mobilize domestic financing for health, and improve quality improvement and accreditation systems for both public and private facilities. RIHSA will train healthcare workers at the decentralized level to implement quality standards of care and strengthen Rwanda&apos;s Health Management Information System (HMIS). RIHSA will work closely with the Ministry of Health, Rwanda Social Security Board, and other entities to improve Rwanda&apos;s Community Based Health Insurance (CBHI) management system, ultimately, allowing CBHI to become the bridge for universal healthcare..Rwanda has made great strides in improving its health system through implementation of progressive policies, such as the CBHI and the HMIS, and close coordination with donors. Building on the U.S. government&apos;s investments in Rwanda&apos;s health system, RIHSA will institutionalize and strengthen advances in Rwanda&apos;s health system for sustainability, contributing to Rwanda&apos;s quest for sustainable development..</narrative>
  </description>
